<Project>

  <!--
    Where the KSA assemblies the mod compiles against come from.

    They are RocketWerkz's copyrighted game files and cannot be committed here, so this resolves
    a folder rather than keeping copies. First match wins:

      1. KSA_DLL_DIR, as a property or an environment variable. This is what CI uses, pointing
         at a checkout of the private ksa-game-assemblies repository. It is also the escape
         hatch for any install this file does not guess.
      2. Import/, populated by tools/sync-import.sh. The long-standing local arrangement.
      3. A ksa-game-assemblies checkout sitting next to this repository - clone both and go,
         with nothing to configure.
      4. The game install itself. Windows, then native Linux, then WSL.

    Tier 4 used to be "Windows, otherwise WSL", which quietly assumed that every non-Windows
    developer was on WSL: a native Linux contributor got /mnt/c/... , a path that cannot exist on
    their machine, and no hint that KSA_DLL_DIR was the way out. The Linux locations below are
    the common ones; anything else still works via KSA_DLL_DIR, which the error at the bottom
    now actually says.
  -->
  <PropertyGroup>
    <KsaDllDir Condition="'$(KsaDllDir)' == '' AND '$(KSA_DLL_DIR)' != ''">$([MSBuild]::EnsureTrailingSlash('$(KSA_DLL_DIR)'))</KsaDllDir>
    <KsaDllDir Condition="'$(KsaDllDir)' == '' AND Exists('$(MSBuildThisFileDirectory)Import/KSA.dll')">$(MSBuildThisFileDirectory)Import/</KsaDllDir>
    <KsaDllDir Condition="'$(KsaDllDir)' == '' AND Exists('$(MSBuildThisFileDirectory)../ksa-game-assemblies/current/dll/KSA.dll')">$(MSBuildThisFileDirectory)../ksa-game-assemblies/current/dll/</KsaDllDir>

    <!-- Windows -->
    <KsaDllDir Condition="'$(KsaDllDir)' == '' AND Exists('C:\Program Files\Kitten Space Agency\KSA.dll')">C:\Program Files\Kitten Space Agency\</KsaDllDir>

    <!-- Native Linux and macOS: Steam in both its usual homes, then the obvious manual spots. -->
    <KsaDllDir Condition="'$(KsaDllDir)' == '' AND Exists('$(HOME)/.steam/steam/steamapps/common/Kitten Space Agency/KSA.dll')">$(HOME)/.steam/steam/steamapps/common/Kitten Space Agency/</KsaDllDir>
    <KsaDllDir Condition="'$(KsaDllDir)' == '' AND Exists('$(HOME)/.local/share/Steam/steamapps/common/Kitten Space Agency/KSA.dll')">$(HOME)/.local/share/Steam/steamapps/common/Kitten Space Agency/</KsaDllDir>
    <KsaDllDir Condition="'$(KsaDllDir)' == '' AND Exists('$(HOME)/Games/Kitten Space Agency/KSA.dll')">$(HOME)/Games/Kitten Space Agency/</KsaDllDir>
    <KsaDllDir Condition="'$(KsaDllDir)' == '' AND Exists('$(HOME)/Kitten Space Agency/KSA.dll')">$(HOME)/Kitten Space Agency/</KsaDllDir>

    <!-- WSL, last: this path exists only there, so probing it earlier would shadow a real install. -->
    <KsaDllDir Condition="'$(KsaDllDir)' == '' AND Exists('/mnt/c/Program Files/Kitten Space Agency/KSA.dll')">/mnt/c/Program Files/Kitten Space Agency/</KsaDllDir>

    <HaveKsaAssemblies>false</HaveKsaAssemblies>
    <HaveKsaAssemblies Condition="'$(KsaDllDir)' != '' AND Exists('$(KsaDllDir)KSA.dll')">true</HaveKsaAssemblies>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <!--
    The check the comment above has always promised and never had. HaveKsaAssemblies was computed
    and then read by nothing, so a contributor with no KSA install got a wall of "type or
    namespace not found" that says nothing about the real problem.

    A target rather than a plain error so it only fires on a real build, and only for the projects
    that actually need the game - `dotnet restore` and IDE load stay quiet.
  -->
  <Target Name="AirDefenceCheckKsaAssemblies"
          BeforeTargets="CoreCompile"
          Condition="'$(HaveKsaAssemblies)' != 'true' AND '$(AirDefenceNeedsKsa)' != 'false'">
    <Error Text="
KSA's assemblies were not found, so this project cannot compile.

Looked in (first match wins):
  KSA_DLL_DIR                     $(KSA_DLL_DIR)
  Import/                         $(MSBuildThisFileDirectory)Import/
  ../ksa-game-assemblies          $(MSBuildThisFileDirectory)../ksa-game-assemblies/current/dll/
  a KSA install                   Windows, Steam on Linux, ~/Games, ~/, or WSL's /mnt/c

Pick whichever fits:
  * Own KSA?    KSA_DLL_DIR=/path/to/Kitten Space Agency ./tools/build.sh
                ...or ./tools/sync-import.sh to copy them into Import/ once.
  * Have the private mirror? Clone ksa-game-assemblies next to this repository.

They are RocketWerkz's copyrighted files: keep your own copy, never commit or publish one.
Run ./tools/doctor.sh for a full check of this machine's setup." />
  </Target>

</Project>
